# ============================================================
#  THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC.
#  https://github.com/greersome/gbt-trail-map  (GitHub Pages)
#
#  Anything committed here is visible to anyone, forever —
#  deleting a file later does NOT un-publish it.
#
#  This file therefore works DENY-BY-DEFAULT: everything is
#  ignored unless it is explicitly allowed below.
#
#  TO PUBLISH A NEW FILE, add an explicit "!" line for it, e.g.
#      !/new-page.html
#  Then confirm before committing:
#      git status --short
#      git check-ignore -v <file>     # should print nothing
#
#  This directory is also used as a working folder for FGBT
#  documents, contact exports and downloads. None of that
#  belongs on the public web. Deny-by-default is what keeps a
#  stray `git add -A` from publishing it.
# ============================================================

# Ignore everything by default.
*

# --- Allowed: the published site ---------------------------
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/index.html
!/alt-instrument-version.html

# ============================================================
#  Explicitly called out so the intent survives this file
#  being edited later. These must NEVER be committed:
#
#   FGBT_contacts.csv        25 volunteer records — name, email,
#                            two phones, street address, city,
#                            postal code, organization, title
#   FGBTcontacts.vcf         26 vCards, same data
#   kate-contact.vcf         named individual
#   Home Sleep Study.ics     personal medical appointment
#   *.docx / *.pdf           FGBT strategic plan drafts
#   drive-download-*.zip     bulk Drive exports
#   traildayinformation*     volunteer packets
#
#  The deny-by-default rule above already covers these. The
#  list is here so that anyone loosening the rule can see what
#  it was protecting.
# ============================================================
